-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",405,{
[12929]="7003FBC6\n1\tCatch Lamedon Salmon (total: 6)\tLamedon Salmon can be found north of Calembel in Lamedon in disturbed waters. Torchuil asked you to catch salmon to help stock the larders for the winter.\n2\tTalk to Torchuil\tTorchuil is in Dol Amroth. Torchuil will be pleased to see the amount of salmon you have caught.\n",
[12930]="7004CE93\n1\tRescue Sangemêkh Turáh\tFind and rescue Sangemêkh Turáh from the Jangovar camp, on the eastern side of the Long Lake.\n2\tTalk to Sangemêkh Turáh\tYou should talk to Turáh in the Jangovar camp, on the eastern side of the Long Lake.\n3\tFind and free the other Chayasír captives in the Jangovar camp, on the eastern side of the Long Lake.\t\n4\tMeet Turáh back at the camps\tYou have freed Turáh and the other Chayasír and should meet them back at the refugee camps, in the hills east of Dale.\n",
[12931]="70044645\n1\tDestroy Cave-lizard nests (total: 8)\030Defeat Old Stone-tail\tCave-lizard nests and Old Stone-tail can be found within the cisterns. You should remove the cave-lizard infestation from the cisterns.\n2\tSpeak with Rathon\tRathon can be found outside the cistern entrance on the Fourth Circle of Minas Tirith. You should speak with Rathon.\n",
[12932]="70036EDC\n1\tAsk Éomer how you can help the Westfold\tÉomer is at Helm's Gate. You should speak with Éomer.\n2\tAsk Aragorn how you can help the Westfold\tAragorn is at Helm's Gate. You should speak with Aragorn.\n3\tTake leave of King Théoden\tThéoden is at Helm's Gate. You should speak with Théoden.\n",
[12933]="7001CC52\n1\tExamine the blank gravestone more closely this time\tThe blank gravestone is in the graveyard to the south of Audaghaim and the Haunted Inn. You should search the area of the uninformative gravestone again for anything you may have missed.\n2\tTalk to Prestadír at the Haunted Inn\tPrestadír is at the Haunted Inn in the Dourstocks, north of the graveyard. You should tell Prestadír of your encounter with the condemned Record-keeper who appeared when you searched his grave.\n",
[12934]="70008663\n1\tFind Arngrim\tArngrim is seeking mithril atop a ridge on the very southern reaches of Imlad Balchorth, north of Gabilshathûr. Bothwar is concerned that Arngrim, slightly befuddled at the best of times, might have gotten himself into trouble in the southern reaches of Imlad Balchorth.\n2\tTalk to Bothwar\tBothwar is on the bridge in the middle of Gabilshathûr, south of Imlad Balchorth. You have returned Arngrim to his senses and should report back to Bothwar.\n",
[12935]="70054657\n1\tTalk to Felgúr\tLegolas has asked you to unbind Felgúr and send him on his mission. You should talk to Felgúr in Echad Taerdim.\n2\tFind the Ungoledain with Felgúr\tFelgúr has begun tracking the other Ungoledain. You should travel with Felgúr.\n3\tFind the Ungoledain with Felgúr\tFelgúr has begun tracking the other Ungoledain. You should travel with Felgúr.\n4\tFind the Ungoledain with Felgúr\tFelgúr has begun tracking the other Ungoledain. You should travel with Felgúr.\n5\tFind the Ungoledain with Felgúr\tFelgúr has begun tracking the other Ungoledain. You should travel with Felgúr.\n6\tTalk to Legolas\tLegolas has appeared near an Uruk camp in eastern Cirith Ungol. You should talk to Legolas.\n7\tTalk to Felgúr\tFelgúr would like to speak with you. You should talk to Felgúr.\n8\tFind Rûkhor's first orders to Zabothak\030Find Rûkhor's second orders to Zabothak\030Find Rûkhor's third orders to Zabothak\030Find Rûkhor's fourth orders to Zabothak\tLegolas has asked you to find evidence of Rûkhor's plans in Kaslokroz. You should find written orders to the Uruk lieutenants.\n9\tTalk to Legolas\tLegolas is waiting near Kaslokroz. You should talk to Legolas.\n",
[12936]="7004186C\n1\tBury slain Gondorians in Lornost\tYou have come upon a massacre in Lornost, and should now bury the dead.\n2\tBury slain Gondorians in Lornost (total: 8)\tSlain Gondorians can be found throughout Lornost in eastern Lebennin. You have discovered the grim aftermath of a slaughter in Lornost and should bury the people of the fallen settlement so that they may have some dignity in death.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have buried all of the people of Lornost.\n",
[12937]="700686B0\n1\tConfront Akhâd\030Confront Sikaru\030Confront Krûha\030Confront Jakham\030Confront Grizagâr\030Confront Medêshi\tMedêshi, Grizagâr, Jakham, Krûha, Sikaru, and Akhâd can be found throughout the Sail-haven, either upon the decks of their ships in the harbour or lurking at one of the local taverns. Eshmun has asked you to find, confront, and defeat Balakhôr the Scourge's loyal captains in Umbar Baharbêl.\n2\tTalk to Eshmun at the Harbour-warden's Tower\tEshmun, Captain of the Haven, can be found at the Harbour-warden's Tower in the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl. You have defeated all of Balakhôr the Scourge's loyal captains in the Sail-haven. You should return to Eshmun.\n",
[12938]="70041182\n1\tCollect orders of the Scourge from Umbarrim (total: 3)\tUmbarrim can be found along the path and in the main encampment in Tarlang's Crown. Based on what you discovered in Azruthor's personal notes, it is likely that the Umbarrim bear orders from the Scourge himself.\n2\tTalk to Harnion\tHarnion can be found along the road through Tarlang's Crown, to the north of Edhellond in Belfalas. You have recovered several pages of the Scourge's orders, and should now bring them to Harnion.\n",
[12939]="70001793\n1\tDefeat goblins (total: 8)\030Destroy goblin-tents (total: 6)\tThe goblin camp is east of Amon Raith, on the southern hills of Annúndir. You should enter the goblin camp and defeat a number of goblins there.\n2\tTalk to Amarion\tThe Ranger Amarion is at Amon Raith, west of Annúndir. Amarion is waiting to hear about your attack on the goblins of Annúndir.\n",
[12940]="70016708\n1\tPlace the bag of remains on the crate\tThe crate is near the Chittering Hole, south-east of the Orc-watch. Ingifast wants you to place the bag containing the remains of the previous White Hand expedition on a raised surface, such as a crate, near a patrol-route often used by White Hand scouts. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tTalk to Ingifast in the Orc-watch\tIngifast is at the Orc-watch, north-west of the Chittering Hole. Ingifast will be pleased to hear the evidence has been placed on the crate for the scout to find.\n",
[12941]="70032C25\n1\tFind the Moria tribe report\030Find the White Hand tribe report\tThe scouting report is hidden in each tribe's camp. Each tribe has been scouting the other's defences, locations of strategic points, and general mining operations.\n2\tReturn reports to Ingifast near the Orc-watch\tIngifast's camp is on the stairs near Orc-watch. Ingifast will be pleased to see the reports that you have gathered.\n",
[12942]="70061BA9\n1\tTalk to Eluna at Bloodhollow to the east\tEluna will travel to a small area east of the Warg camp known as Bloodhollow. Meet Eluna east of Bloodhollow.\n",
[12943]="70041038\n1\tFind the beach upon which the Corsairs have landed\tThe Corsairs have landed on a beach south-west of Dol Amroth. Jajax has asked you to search for Abedec at the beach-side landing spot, while he searches some ruins to the south.\n2\tLook for Abedec from the south-eastern watch-tower\030Look for Abedec from the north-western watch-tower\tGood vantage points for searching for signs of Abedec can be found atop the watch-towers in Hashadîr, south-west of Dol Amroth. You should climb the watch-towers on the beach and look for signs of Abedec.\n3\tMeet Jajax at the cross-roads\tJajax's meeting place is where the roads meet between the two Corsair encampments -- one leads from the south-west, from Hashadîr, and the other leads from the ruins to the south. You should meet Jajax at the cross-roads.\n4\tSearch for Jajax in the ruins to the south\tJajax is likely somewhere in the ruins to the south of Dol Amroth. You should search for Jajax, for he is probably in need of rescue.\n",
[12944]="700662B2\n1\tFind Dolvir near Abadec's Watch\tGilanor has sent you to find Dolvir. Dolvir may be somewhere near Abadec's Watch, which lies south-west of Ost Lontir.\n2\tTalk to Dolvir\tYou have found an injured Dolvir amongst the trees north of Abadec's Watch. You should make sure he's alright.\n",
[12945]="700442F3\n1\tLook around for signs of Dúneth at the first farmhouse\030Look around for signs of Dúneth at the second farmhouse\030Look around for signs of Dúneth at the third farmhouse\030Look around for signs of Dúneth at the fourth farmhouse\030Find and defeat the captain at Parth Lisc\030Find and defeat the captain at Parth Duin\tParth Lisc is located in north-eastern Talath Anor and Parth Duin is located in eastern Talath Anor. You should travel to the Parth Lisc and Parth Duin and search for Dúneth.\n2\tTalk to Tolwin\tTolwin can be found in the hall of Crithost. You should speak with Tolwin.\n",
[12946]="70044309\n1\tSearch Parth Forant for Dúneth\tParth Forant is located in Talath Anor on the banks of the River Forant. Your should search Parth Forant for Dúneth.\n2\tSpeak with Tolwin\tSpeak with Tolwin.\n3\tTravel to Parth Gladló\tParth Gladló is located in southern Talath Anor. Your best chance at finding Dúneth is searching Parth Gladló.\n4\tLook around for signs of Dúneth at the first farmhouse\030Look around for signs of Dúneth at the second farmhouse\tParth Gladló is located in southern Talath Anor. You should search buildings at Parth Gladló.\n5\tFind and defeat Gúrdru\tGúrdru can be found in Parth Gladló. You should find and defeat Gúrdru.\n6\tEnter the woods in pursuit of the mysterious figure\tThe woods can be found in eastern Talath Anor. You should follow the mysterious figure into the woods.\n7\tFollow the trail of footprints deeper into the woods\tThe trail of footsteps leads deeper into the woods. You should follow the trail to find this mysterious figure.\n8\tSpeak with Dúneth\tDúneth is located at her camp. You should speak with Dúneth.\n9\tSpeak with Tolwin\tSpeak with Tolwin.\n",
[12947]="7004135D\n1\tSearch for signs of a conflict in western Dor-en-Ernil\tErchar and Herion were last seen riding out to the fields in the western part of Dor-en-Ernil. You should search for signs of a conflict.\n2\tExamine the set of footprints\tThe ground shows signs of a conflict between Gondorians and Corsairs. You should examine the prints at the edge of the battleground.\n3\tFind and examine the next set of prints\tYou should examine any prints you find in the dirt.\n4\tFind and examine the next set of prints\tYou should examine any prints you find in the dirt.\n5\tSeek out Erchar and his men\tErchar and his men must be hiding somewhere north-west of here in Dor-en-Ernil. You should search for Erchar's camp.\n6\tSpeak with Erchar at his encampment\tErchar can be found in his encampment in the western end of Dor-en-Ernil. Talk to Erchar and bring news of his brother's plea for return.\n7\tErchar's men can be found in Erchar's encampment. Challenge Gondorian soldiers to defend their homeland.\t\n8\tTalk to Erchar at his encampment\tErchar can be found at his encampment in the western end of Dor-en-Ernil. Speak with Erchar.\n",
[12948]="70000177\n1\tFind Bob's daughter, Lalia\tAccording to Butterbur's tale, the Barrow of the Last Prince lies between Northern Barrow and the Dead Spire, near a large standing stone. Bob has asked you to search the Barrow-downs for his missing daughter, who likely has come here in search of the fabled \"Last Prince.\"\n",
[12949]="70039F9E\n1\tFind Meregyth\tMeregyth was last seen heading along the road south towards Beaconwatch. Thane Sparhafoc asked you to find Meregyth and watch over her.\n2\tFollow the road that leads south and look for Meregyth\tMeregyth was last seen heading along the road south towards Beaconwatch. Thane Sparhafoc asked you to find Meregyth and watch over her.\n3\tLook for the trail of flowers Meregyth left behind\tThe trail of flowers leads to the south. It is possible that Meregyth is leaving a trail in order to locate her. She may be in trouble after all. You should continue following the flowers in hopes of locating Meregyth.\n4\tLook for the trail of flowers Meregyth left behind\tThe trail of flowers leads to the south. It is very clear that Meregyth is leaving a trail in order to locate her. She may be in trouble after all. You should continue following the flowers in hopes of locating Meregyth.\n5\tFollow Meregyth's trail along the stream\tThe trail of flowers goes off the road and runs adjacent to the stream. You should continue to follow Meregyth's trail.\n6\tFollow the narrow path that leads behind the waterfall\tThe trail of flowers goes up a narrow path that leads behind the waterfall. You should follow the path that winds around the waterfall.\n7\tFree Meregyth\tIt is clear now that Meregyth was taken by the Orcs. You should find her and free her from the clutches of the Orcs.\n",
[12950]="700490DB\n1\tTalk to Ingold\tIngold can be found at the Ruins of Díngarth. You should speak with Ingold to learn anything you can about Sapakár.\n2\tLook Around for signs of Sapakár at his last known location\tYou should travel to the last known location of Sapakár.\n3\tEnter Barad-dûr and seek out Sapakár\tSapakár can be found somewhere in Barad-dûr. You should seek out Sapakár.\n4\tSeek out Sapakár\tSapakár can be found deep within the bones of Barad-dûr. You should seek out Sapakár.\n5\tTalk to Sapakár\tSapakár can be found somewhere in Barad-dûr. You should confront Sapakár.\n",
[12951]="700453DB\n1\tLook Around for any clues as to Shákrug's whereabouts\tThe spot where Bhai-buri-Ghân was killed can be found east of Amon Dîn, outside of the Drúadan Forest. You should hike to the place where Bhai-buri-Ghân was killed by Shákrug.\n2\tFollow the Orc prints to see where they lead\tYou should follow the Orc prints to see where they lead.\n3\tFind Shákrug's stronghold\tMaudhúl Grak can be found in northern Taur Drúadan. You should find Shákrug's stronghold in Maudhúl Grak.\n4\tDefeat the Mordor Key-warden\tThe Mordor Key-warden is located in Maudhúl Grak. You should defeat the Mordor Key-warden.\n",
[12952]="7005D360\n1\tSearch for Tharrkirîn\tTharrkirîn is in northern Gundabad. Gerja has asked you to discover Tharrkirîn.\n2\tTharrkirîn is in northern Clovengap. You have found Tharrkirîn, a plateau with stone-topped display platforms. You should explore the museum.\t\n3\tReturn to Gerja\tGerja is located in Bazanmanar. You should let Gerja know what you found in Tharrkirîn.\n",
[12953]="70035707\n1\tThrymm was hurled north-west by Núrzum. You should look north-west of Scylfig for signs of Thrymm. NOTE: This quest requires emotes.\t\n2\tPick up the object that caught your eye\tThe item that caught your eye (a horn, perhaps) is just to the west of your last vantage point. You should examine the item you spotted in the snow.\n3\tSee if the body on the road below is Thrymm\tA body lies below the horn in the north-western Writhendowns, upon the road. You should investigate the body, for it is likely Thrymm's.\n4\tBring the horn to Cyneberg\tCyneberg is in Scylfig. You should return to Cyneberg and show her the horn.\n5\tBring Thrymm's horn to Gárwig, Reeve of Wildermore\tGárwig, the Reeve of Wildermore, can be found in Forlaw. Cyneberg has asked you to deliver Thrymm's horn to Gárwig.\n",
[12954]="7001A6FA\n1\tCollect unfamiliar plants (total: 10)\030Collect unfamiliar herbs (total: 10)\tPlants can be found growing near the dreadful pool in the Drownholt, south from Estolad Mernael. You should hasten to the pool and collect many herbs there, for these may possess some property that could heal the steed Alagos.\n2\tTalk to Nestawen at Estolad Mernael\tNestawen can be found at Estolad Mernael, tending her sick steed Alagos. You should bring the plants and flowers you collected to Nestawen to see if they can be of any use to her.\n",
[12955]="70030236\n1\tCollect potential medicinal plants (total: 8)\tPlants that have mild anti-poison properties can be found throughout the forest near Léofmar. You should pick medicinal plants in the hope that they will cure Léofmar.\n2\tBring the medicine to Léofmar\tLéofmar is where you left him, sick and dying in the centre of Fangorn's eaves. You should rush the medicine to Léofmar at once.\n",
[12956]="7004A8D2\n1\tCaptain Róglarg can be found in the courtyard of Cirith Ungol. Captain Róglarg plans to direct you to each of the landmarks you must search for the Elf-warrior. You should speak to him.\t\n2\tReport to Captain Róglarg in Cirith Ungol\tCaptain Róglarg can be found in the courtyard of Cirith Ungol. You have patrolled all three landmarks and should now return to Captain Róglarg.\n",
[12957]="7003493A\n1\tTalk to Cyneberg\tCyneberg is at the refugees' hideout in the Whitshaws. You should speak with Cyneberg.\n2\tFind Iothete, the owner of the empty home\tBased on the memories of the townsfolk, Iothete likely headed north into the woods from Dunfast. You should search for Iothete, the man with the empty home.\n",
[12958]="7003468E\n1\tTorwulf asked you to call him to you on your way to Gárferth's Farm. On the road south of Thrymm's Farm is likely a good spot to summon him.\t\n2\tSpeak to Torwulf\tNow that he is with you, speak to Torwulf before heading to Gárferth's Farm.\n3\tFind Gárferth's Farm\tGárferth's Farm is down the road south of Thrymm's Farm.\n4\tTorwulf's father must be on or around Gárferth's Farm somewhere. With many Warg-riders roaming the area, he probably didn't make it far.\t\n5\tWinerad was barely hanging on, but didn't make it. Torwulf is likely in shock from what has happened, but he wants to have a word with you at the location of his father's death.\t\n6\tSpeak with Torwulf back at Thrymm's Farm\tTorwulf has gone back to Thrymm's Farm, and will want to have a word with you.\n",
[12959]="7003467B\n1\tFind Manléof at Gársig's Farm\tGársig's Farm is on the far eastern side of the Fallows, near the Wold.\n2\tCheck on Manléof's injuries and defeat any nearby foes\tManléof, who was left behind at Gársig's Farm, is in very poor condition. He isn't likely to live much longer.\n3\tReturn to Siric at Thrymm's Farm\tManléof didn't survive the encounter with Warg-riders at Gársig's Farm. You should let Siric know what has happened, and he is awaiting your return at Thrymm's Farm.\n",
[12960]="7004A8F9\n1\tPatrol Fennas Gost \"in search of the Elf-warrior\"\tFennas Gost can be found due south of Cirith Ungol in the heights of the Ephel Dúath. Captain Róglarg has asked you to patrol the gate to Imlad Morgul, Fennas Gost, in search of the Elf-warrior on the run in Lhingris. You should travel to Fennas Gost.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have patrolled Fennas Gost.\n",
})
